ed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $C$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1b86265beb6c8430c7d4f28fef542e7feadfce5e025ad03fe9f1e9cb69e8aa"} {"question" "q-32177" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73338c461ad8c65ac6623d7dce9979873dd5ee77ce505d942f8270d9eb203288"} {"question" "q-32177" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1b86265beb6c8430c7d4f28fef542e7feadfce5e025ad03fe9f1e9cb69e8aa"} {"question" "q-32177" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1b86265beb6c8430c7d4f28fef542e7feadfce5e025ad03fe9f1e9cb69e8aa"} {"question" "q-32177" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $C$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1b86265beb6c8430c7d4f28fef542e7feadfce5e025ad03fe9f1e9cb69e8aa"} {"question" "q-42129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find \n$|\\begin{aligned}a & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & b & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|$\ngiven that \n$|\\begin{aligned}a & 2 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}|=-5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1b86265beb6c8430c7d4f28fef542e7feadfce5e025ad03fe9f1e9cb69e8aa"} {"question" "q-42129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we have  a block upper triangular matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}a & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & b & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}a & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & b & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}a & 2 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}|\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1b86265beb6c8430c7d4f28fef542e7feadfce5e025ad03fe9f1e9cb69e8aa"} {"question" "q-42129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73338c461ad8c65ac6623d7dce9979873dd5ee77ce505d942f8270d9eb203288"} {"question" "q-42129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1b86265beb6c8430c7d4f28fef542e7feadfce5e025ad03fe9f1e9cb69e8aa"} {"question" "q-42129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-16"] ["math" "-20"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers