y/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "73338c461ad8c65ac6623d7dce9979873dd5ee77ce505d942f8270d9eb203288"} {"question" "q-42139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1b86265beb6c8430c7d4f28fef542e7feadfce5e025ad03fe9f1e9cb69e8aa"} {"question" "q-42139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1b86265beb6c8430c7d4f28fef542e7feadfce5e025ad03fe9f1e9cb69e8aa"} {"question" "q-42139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1b86265beb6c8430c7d4f28fef542e7feadfce5e025ad03fe9f1e9cb69e8aa"} {"question" "e-9093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A partitioned matrix $M$ contains the following blocks: \n\n- $M_{11},$ which is a $1 \\times 2$ block\n\n- $M_{12},$ which is a $1 \\times 3$ block\n\n- $M_{21},$ which is a $2 \\times 2$ block\n\nFind the dimensions of the block $M_{22}$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/example-9093.json" "file_sha256" "50066e78071bddd114412a024442097850e68873fb8bd16def6e82616e6c0607"} {"question" "e-9093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a matrix of the form\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/assets/2ebec2a87fd922bcbe30ee648e102188b48854abcad34d88cc18695cac67e1bd.png)\n\nTherefore,  $M_{22}$ must be a $2 \\times 3$ block." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/example-9093.json" "file_sha256" "50066e78071bddd114412a024442097850e68873fb8bd16def6e82616e6c0607"} {"question" "e-9094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/assets/a610512000d95e3ed80559431e25501a9d498d342e7c180864720bbeb2ee10d4.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/example-9094.json" "file_sha256" "69714db24aacc1926b40e59cb466ffe9b63b55e853733f7fcc723c93ed384a31"} {"question" "e-9094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A block diagonal matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and all the other blocks contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block diagonal matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/assets/f6e977aff21319bb8e0cbb251d36577966f84060e809e3485f9019e85cd3538e.png)\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/assets/597e27b2f470bc60717eb3341d2f3e87f411c0a4c796a58ee3aa83c691971517.png)\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/example-9094.json" "file_sha256" "69714db24aacc1926b40e59cb466ffe9b63b55e853733f7fcc723c93ed384a31"} {"question" "e-9096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/assets/f9f02df9d1e971ccea2d5abb67f95866bb334e636e5d39ec59d14a617d8f15f0.png)\ngiven that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/assets/58f57ca9a1782c7edc2367b2aed9798e8e2c1eb8318000e6202b3fa0746c6a90.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/example-9096.json" "file_sha256" "25959306f66a705214251c40e37264e87add4e4ad5c5dcdb09daca02280d188b"} {"question" "e-9096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we have  a block upper triangular matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the determinants of the diagonal blocks:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & e & 4 \\\\ 0 & h & 8\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & e & 4 \\\\ 0 & h & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}e & 4 \\\\ h & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/example-9096.json" "file_sha256" "25959306f66a705214251c40e37264e87add4e4ad5c5dcdb09daca02280d188b"}] "usage" {"e-9096" [] "e-9094" [] "e-9093" [] "q-42134" [] "q-32130" []} "basis" 1550 "retractions" [[17592186115666 :question/problem "A partitioned matrix $M$ contains the following blocks:\n\n- $M_{11}$, which is a $3 \\cdot 2$ block\n- $M_{12}$, which is a $3 \\cdot 1$ block\n- $M_{22}$, which is a $2 \\cdot 1$ block\n\nWhat are the dimensions of the block $M_{21}$?"] [17592186115666 :question/answer-fields 17592186113396] [17592186115745 :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186115067 :question/problem "A partitioned matrix $M$ contains the following blocks:\n\n- $M_{11}$, which is a $1 \\times 2$ block\n- $M_{12}$, which is a $1 \\times 3$ block\n- $M_{21}$, which is a $2 \\times 2$ block\n\nFind the dimensions of the block $M_{22}$."] [17592186115067 :question/worked-solution "We have a matrix of the form\n$\\begin{bmatrix}M_{11} & M_{12} \\\\ M_{21} & M_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nTherefore, $M_{22}$ must be a $2 \\times 3$ block."] [17592186115068 :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186115068 :question/worked-solution "A block diagonal matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and all the other blocks contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block diagonal matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{bmatrix}$\n- $B$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n- $C$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n$C = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only.\""] [17592186115069 :question/problem "Find\n$\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & e & 4 \\\\ 0 & h & 8\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}e & 4 \\\\ h & 8\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186115069 :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a block upper triangular matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the determinants of the diagonal blocks:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & e & 4 \\\\ 0 & h & 8\\end{vmatrix} &= \\begin{vmatrix}7 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & e & 4 \\\\ 0 & h & 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 7 \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}e & 4 \\\\ h & 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 7 \\cdot 6 \\\\\n&= 42\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186113397 17592186113398 17592186113399 17592186113400 17592186113401 17592186113842 17592186113843 17592186113844 17592186113845 17592186113846] "immutable_fields" [[17592186113396 :answer-field/correct] [17592186113396 :answer-field/id] [17592186113396 :answer-field/key] [17592186113396 :answer-field/type] [17592186113841 :answer-field/correct] [17592186113841 :answer-field/id] [17592186113841 :answer-field/key] [17592186113841 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
